# Resneo Mobile App — Cursor Rules

## Project Context

This is the React Native mobile app for Resneo, a booking and business 
management SaaS platform for Northern Ireland businesses (salons, restaurants, 
practitioners). It shares a backend with the Resneo web app but is a 
separate codebase.

Target users: business owners and staff (NOT end customers booking 
appointments). Primary use case: a salon owner glancing at today's diary 
behind the counter, taking a quick booking when someone walks in, getting 
push notifications for new bookings.

The developer (Andrew) is a beginner. Explain non-obvious choices in 
comments. Prefer clear, readable code over clever code. When introducing a 
new pattern or library, briefly explain why in a comment.

## Tech Stack — Use These, Not Alternatives

- React Native via Expo (SDK 52+)
- Expo Router for file-based navigation (NOT React Navigation directly)
- TypeScript, strict mode, NO `any` types
- Supabase (@supabase/supabase-js) for backend, auth, and database
- expo-secure-store for auth tokens (NOT AsyncStorage, NOT localStorage)
- TanStack Query (@tanstack/react-query) for server state
- Zod for runtime validation
- date-fns for date manipulation (NOT moment, NOT dayjs)
- react-native-reanimated for animations when needed
- expo-notifications for push

## Critical: This Is Not a Web App

NEVER generate:
- HTML elements (<div>, <span>, <button>, <input>, <a>, <p>, <h1>, etc.)
- className= or CSS classes
- CSS files, Tailwind, or styled-components
- window., document., localStorage, sessionStorage
- href links — use Expo Router's <Link> or router.push()
- <form> with onSubmit — use button onPress handlers

ALWAYS use:
- <View>, <Text>, <Pressable>, <ScrollView>, <TextInput>, <Image>
- StyleSheet.create({...}) or inline style={{...}} objects
- Flexbox for all layout (no Grid — it doesn't exist in RN)
- expo-secure-store for sensitive storage
- expo-router's <Link> and useRouter() for navigation

## Styling Conventions

- Define a central theme in `theme/index.ts` with colors, spacing, typography
- Use StyleSheet.create() at the bottom of component files for component-scoped styles
- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 48 (multiples of 4)
- Use SafeAreaView (from react-native-safe-area-context) for top-level screens
- Touch targets minimum 44x44 (Apple HIG) — important on a phone behind a busy salon counter

## File Structure

app/                    # Expo Router screens (file-based routing)
  (auth)/              # Auth flow group
    sign-in.tsx
    sign-up.tsx
  (tabs)/              # Main tab navigation
    index.tsx          # Today view
    week.tsx
    clients.tsx
    settings.tsx
  booking/[id].tsx     # Booking detail
components/            # Reusable UI components
  ui/                  # Primitive components (Button, Card, Input)
  bookings/            # Domain components
lib/                   # Non-UI logic
  supabase.ts          # Supabase client setup
  queries/             # TanStack Query hooks
  validation/          # Zod schemas
types/                 # Shared TypeScript types
theme/                 # Colors, spacing, typography

## Supabase Patterns

- Use Row Level Security policies — never bypass with service role on the client
- The mobile app uses the same RLS policies as the web app
- For queries, prefer TanStack Query wrappers in lib/queries/ over inline calls
- Auth tokens go in expo-secure-store via Supabase's custom storage option
- Real-time subscriptions are powerful for the Today view — use them for booking updates

## Linked Accounts Context

Resneo supports linked accounts for chair-rental scenarios (multiple 
self-employed stylists sharing a salon). The mobile app must support 
account switching. When implementing anything that touches bookings, 
clients, or settings, consider which account context the user is currently 
in. Use a global account context provider.

## Code Quality

- TypeScript strict mode — fix errors, don't suppress with `any` or `@ts-ignore`
- Always handle loading and error states in UI components, not just success
- All async functions need try/catch when they touch the network
- Validate any data crossing a trust boundary (user input, API responses) with Zod
- Prefer composition over inheritance; prefer hooks over HOCs

## Performance

- Use FlatList (not .map() over ScrollView) for any list of >20 items
- Memoize expensive computations with useMemo
- Wrap callback props with useCallback when passed to memoized children
- Images: use expo-image (NOT React Native's Image) — better caching and performance
- Avoid inline functions in render for performance-sensitive screens

## Comments and Explanations

- Add JSDoc comments to exported functions explaining purpose and params
- Mark TODOs with // TODO(andrew): description
- When implementing something non-obvious (e.g. why a setTimeout, why a ref),
  explain in a comment. Future-me will thank present-me.

## What NOT to Do

- Don't introduce new dependencies without explaining why in the chat first
- Don't generate code that uses lib/supabase with the service role key — anon/publishable key only
- Don't commit `.env.local` or paste secret keys into source files
- Don't read or modify `_reference/reserve-ni` except when explicitly porting API patterns to the mobile app
